{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- backend-go ---'; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- documentation-style ---'; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- relevant knowledge search ---'; rg -n -i 'review dispatch|subreaper|abandoned attempt|delegation release|review run|lingering' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- backend-go ---'; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- documentation-style ---'; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- relevant knowledge search ---'; rg -n -i 'review dispatch|subreaper|abandoned attempt|delegation release|review run|lingering' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":"--- backend-go ---\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n--- documentation-style ---\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n--- relevant knowledge search ---\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:30:- F-R3-07 (low): `on_terminal` fires for `pose delegate review|resume`, not for the deprecated alias `pose review dispatch --via … --apply` nor for a run recorded `stalled`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- review shim ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go | sed -n '1,320p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- process reaper ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,280p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- adapter containment ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- review shim ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go | sed -n '1,320p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- process reaper ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,280p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- adapter containment ---'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\"","aggregated_output":"--- review shim ---\n     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     5\t\t\"time\"\n     6\t)\n     7\t\n     8\t// The review run shim (spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes,\n     9\t// review rounds 6 and 8): a descendant of the reviewer that leaves the\n    10\t// adapter's process group, starts its own session and clears its environment\n    11\t// matches neither the group kill nor the sealed-checkout entry. Making the\n    12\t// dispatcher a child subreaper caught it, but a subreaper is process-wide:\n    13\t// in the dispatching process it also adopted and ended children other code\n    14\t// started there (a detached delegation), and reaped processes another\n    15\t// goroutine was waiting for. The dispatcher therefore starts the adapter\n    16\t// through a shim, the same executable re-entered with ReviewShimArg, which\n    17\t// makes itself the subreaper, runs the adapter, and, once it exits, ends\n    18\t// every process left in its subtree. The shim has no other children, so\n    19\t// everything it adopts is the run's. A timeout asks the shim to stop with\n    20\t// SIGTERM, and the death of the dispatcher delivers it the same signal: in\n    21\t// both cases it ends the subtree before it exits (review round 8, N3, N4).\n    22\t\n    23\t// reviewReapWait bounds how long ending the run's leftover processes takes.\n    24\tconst reviewReapWait = 5 * time.Second\n    25\t\n    26\t// ReviewShimArg is the first argument that runs the executable as a review\n    27\t// run shim instead of the CLI.\n    28\tconst ReviewShimArg = \"__pose-review-run-shim\"\n    29\t\n    30\t// ReviewShimReportEnv tells the shim that the dispatcher passed it a report\n    31\t// pipe as file descriptor 3, and names the dispatcher's pid. The report never\n    32\t// goes to a path the reviewer can write (review round 8, N2).\n    33\tconst ReviewShimReportEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_SHIM_REPORT\"\n    34\t\n    35\t// ReviewShimAvailable says the running executable handles ReviewShimArg. It\n    36\t// is set by the pose command and by the test binaries that dispatch; any\n    37\t// other embedder starts the adapter directly, without the shim.\n    38\tvar ReviewShimAvailable = false\n    39\t\n    40\t// reviewShimReport is what the shim found after the adapter exited.\n    41\ttype reviewShimReport struct {\n    42\t\tEnded      []string `json:\"ended\"`\n    43\t\tEndedTotal int      `json:\"ended_total\"`\n    44\t\tError      string   `json:\"error,omitempty\"`\n    45\t}\n    46\t\n    47\t// reviewShimReportMaxPids bounds the pids a report lists; EndedTotal counts\n    48\t// them all. A full report stays far below the dispatcher's read bound.\n    49\tconst reviewShimReportMaxPids = 1000\n    50\t\n    51\t// boundedReviewShimReport encodes r within the dispatcher's read bound, so\n    52\t// the dispatcher always reads it whole (review round 9, N2).\n    53\tfunc boundedReviewShimReport(r reviewShimReport) []byte {\n    54\t\tr.EndedTotal = len(r.Ended)\n    55\t\tif len(r.Ended) > reviewShimReportMaxPids {\n    56\t\t\tr.Ended = r.Ended[:reviewShimReportMaxPids]\n    57\t\t}\n    58\t\tif len(r.Error) > 4096 {\n    59\t\t\tr.Error = r.Error[:4096]\n    60\t\t}\n    61\t\traw, _ := json.Marshal(r)\n    62\t\treturn raw\n    63\t}\n     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     7\t\t\"errors\"\n     8\t\t\"fmt\"\n     9\t\t\"os\"\n    10\t\t\"os/exec\"\n    11\t\t\"os/signal\"\n    12\t\t\"strconv\"\n    13\t\t\"strings\"\n    14\t\t\"syscall\"\n    15\t\t\"time\"\n    16\t\n    17\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    18\t)\n    19\t\n    20\t// RunReviewShim runs args (the adapter's path, then its argv) as the shim's\n    21\t// only child, waits for it or for SIGTERM, ends every process left in the\n    22\t// shim's subtree and returns the adapter's exit status.\n    23\tfunc RunReviewShim(args []string) int {\n    24\t\treport := reviewShimReport{}\n    25\t\tvar reportFile *os.File\n    26\t\tparent := 0\n    27\t\tif value := os.Getenv(ReviewShimReportEnv); value != \"\" {\n    28\t\t\tparent, _ = strconv.Atoi(value)\n    29\t\t\t// The report pipe is the shim's alone: the adapter never inherits it.\n    30\t\t\tsyscall.CloseOnExec(3)\n    31\t\t\treportFile = os.NewFile(3, \"pose-review-shim-report\")\n    32\t\t}\n    33\t\t_ = os.Unsetenv(ReviewShimReportEnv)\n    34\t\twrite := func() {\n    35\t\t\tif reportFile == nil {\n    36\t\t\t\treturn\n    37\t\t\t}\n    38\t\t\traw := boundedReviewShimReport(report)\n    39\t\t\t_, _ = reportFile.Write(raw)\n    40\t\t\t_ = reportFile.Close()\n    41\t\t}\n    42\t\tif len(args) < 2 {\n    43\t\t\treport.Error = \"the review shim was given no adapter\"\n    44\t\t\twrite()\n    45\t\t\treturn 125\n    46\t\t}\n    47\t\tstop := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    48\t\tsignal.Notify(stop, syscall.SIGTERM)\n    49\t\t// The dispatcher's death stops the shim the same way as a timeout.\n    50\t\tif err := unix.Prctl(unix.PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, uintptr(syscall.SIGTERM), 0, 0, 0); err != nil {\n    51\t\t\treport.Error = \"the shim could not follow its dispatcher: \" + err.Error()\n    52\t\t\twrite()\n    53\t\t\treturn 125\n    54\t\t}\n    55\t\tif parent != 0 && os.Getppid() != parent {\n    56\t\t\treport.Error = \"the dispatcher ended before the shim started\"\n    57\t\t\twrite()\n    58\t\t\treturn 125\n    59\t\t}\n    60\t\tif err := unix.Prctl(unix.PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER, 1, 0, 0, 0); err != nil {\n    61\t\t\treport.Error = \"the shim could not become the subreaper of the run: \" + err.Error()\n    62\t\t\twrite()\n    63\t\t\treturn 125\n    64\t\t}\n    65\t\tcmd := &exec.Cmd{Path: args[0], Args: args[1:], Stdin: os.Stdin, Stdout: os.Stdout, Stderr: os.Stderr, Env: os.Environ()}\n    66\t\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n    67\t\t\treport.Error = \"the adapter could not run: \" + err.Error()\n    68\t\t\twrite()\n    69\t\t\treturn 127\n    70\t\t}\n    71\t\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n    72\t\tgo func() { done <- cmd.Wait() }()\n    73\t\tcode, stopped := 0, false\n    74\t\tvar signaled syscall.Signal\n    75\t\tselect {\n    76\t\tcase err := <-done:\n    77\t\t\tvar exit *exec.ExitError\n    78\t\t\tif errors.As(err, &exit) {\n    79\t\t\t\tif status, ok := exit.Sys().(syscall.WaitStatus); ok && status.Signaled() {\n    80\t\t\t\t\tsignaled, code = status.Signal(), 128+int(status.Signal())\n    81\t\t\t\t} else {\n    82\t\t\t\t\tcode = exit.ExitCode()\n    83\t\t\t\t}\n    84\t\t\t} else if err != nil {\n    85\t\t\t\treport.Error = \"the adapter's end could not be read: \" + err.Error()\n    86\t\t\t}\n    87\t\tcase <-stop:\n    88\t\t\tstopped, code = true, 128+int(syscall.SIGTERM)\n    89\t\t}\n    90\t\tended, err := reapShimSubtree()\n    91\t\treport.Ended = ended\n    92\t\tif err != nil && report.Error == \"\" {\n    93\t\t\treport.Error = err.Error()\n    94\t\t}\n    95\t\twrite()\n    96\t\tif stopped {\n    97\t\t\treturn code\n    98\t\t}\n    99\t\t// An adapter ended by a signal is reported as ended by it: the shim ends\n   100\t\t// itself the same way, so the dispatcher reads what it would have read\n   101\t\t// without the shim.\n   102\t\tif signaled != 0 {\n   103\t\t\tsignal.Reset(signaled)\n   104\t\t\t_ = syscall.Kill(os.Getpid(), signaled)\n   105\t\t\ttime.Sleep(time.Second)\n   106\t\t}\n   107\t\treturn code\n   108\t}\n   109\t\n   110\t// stopReviewShim asks a running shim to end its subtree and exit.\n   111\tfunc stopReviewShim(cmd *exec.Cmd) func() error {\n   112\t\treturn func() error { return cmd.Process.Signal(syscall.SIGTERM) }\n   113\t}\n   114\t\n   115\t// reapShimSubtree ends and reaps every child of the shim, including the\n   116\t// orphans its subreaper status adopted, until none is left.\n   117\tfunc reapShimSubtree() ([]string, error) {\n   118\t\tself := os.Getpid()\n   119\t\tvar ended []string\n   120\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n   121\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n   122\t\t// A process that cannot be inspected or ended is not a reason to stop:\n   123\t\t// the others are still ended, and the problem is reported at the end\n   124\t\t// (review round 9, N3).\n   125\t\tvar problems []string\n   126\t\tnote := func(err error) {\n   127\t\t\tif len(problems) < 8 {\n   128\t\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, err.Error())\n   129\t\t\t}\n   130\t\t}\n   131\t\tfor {\n   132\t\t\tchildren := 0\n   133\t\t\tproblems = problems[:0]\n   134\t\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n   135\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   136\t\t\t\tnote(fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err))\n   137\t\t\t}\n   138\t\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   139\t\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n   140\t\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n   141\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   142\t\t\t\t}\n   143\t\t\t\tst, err := readShimProcStat(pid)\n   144\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) {\n   145\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   146\t\t\t\t}\n   147\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   148\t\t\t\t\t// A process of another user is never the run's: with procfs\n   149\t\t\t\t\t// mounted hidepid it is visible and unreadable (review round 10,\n   150\t\t\t\t\t// N1). Only one of this user is an unknown that may be the run's.\n   151\t\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) || oerr == nil && owner != os.Getuid() {\n   152\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   153\t\t\t\t\t}\n   154\t\t\t\t\tchildren++\n   155\t\t\t\t\tnote(fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err))\n   156\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   157\t\t\t\t}\n   158\t\t\t\tif st.ppid != self {\n   159\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   160\t\t\t\t}\n   161\t\t\t\tchildren++\n   162\t\t\t\tif !st.zombie {\n   163\t\t\t\t\t// A pid is reported ended only once its signal was delivered\n   164\t\t\t\t\t// (review round 10, N3).\n   165\t\t\t\t\tif delivered, err := killPinnedChild(pid, self); err != nil {\n   166\t\t\t\t\t\tnote(err)\n   167\t\t\t\t\t} else if delivered {\n   168\t\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n   169\t\t\t\t\t}\n   170\t\t\t\t}\n   171\t\t\t}\n   172\t\t\tfor {\n   173\t\t\t\tpid, err := unix.Wait4(-1, nil, unix.WNOHANG, nil)\n   174\t\t\t\tif pid <= 0 || err != nil {\n   175\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   176\t\t\t\t}\n   177\t\t\t\t// A pid is reported ended once it was signalled and reaped\n   178\t\t\t\t// (review round 12, N2).\n   179\t\t\t\tif seen[pid] {\n   180\t\t\t\t\tdelete(seen, pid)\n   181\t\t\t\t\tended = append(ended, strconv.Itoa(pid))\n   182\t\t\t\t}\n   183\t\t\t}\n   184\t\t\tif children == 0 && len(problems) == 0 {\n   185\t\t\t\treturn ended, nil\n   186\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n   188\t\t\t\treturn ended, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended: %s\", children, strings.Join(problems, \"; \"))\n   189\t\t\t}\n   190\t\t\ttime.Sleep(20 * time.Millisecond)\n   191\t\t}\n   192\t}\n   193\t\n   194\ttype shimProcStat struct {\n   195\t\tppid   int\n   196\t\tzombie bool\n   197\t}\n   198\t\n   199\tfunc readShimProcStat(pid int) (shimProcStat, error) {\n   200\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(\"/proc/\" + strconv.Itoa(pid) + \"/stat\")\n   201\t\tif err != nil {\n   202\t\t\treturn shimProcStat{}, err\n   203\t\t}\n   204\t\ttext := string(raw)\n   205\t\tend := strings.LastIndexByte(text, ')')\n   206\t\tif end < 0 {\n   207\t\t\treturn shimProcStat{}, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d stat is unreadable\", pid)\n   208\t\t}\n   209\t\tf := strings.Fields(text[end+1:])\n   210\t\tif len(f) < 2 {\n   211\t\t\treturn shimProcStat{}, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d stat is unreadable\", pid)\n   212\t\t}\n   213\t\tppid, err := strconv.Atoi(f[1])\n   214\t\tif err != nil {\n   215\t\t\treturn shimProcStat{}, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d stat is unreadable\", pid)\n   216\t\t}\n   217\t\treturn shimProcStat{ppid: ppid, zombie: f[0] == \"Z\"}, nil\n   218\t}\n   219\t\n   220\t// killPinnedChild signals pid through a pidfd while it is still a child of\n   221\t// parent: a pid reused by an unrelated process is never signalled. It says\n   222\t// whether the signal reached the process; one that already ended was not\n   223\t// ended by the shim and is not reported (review round 11, N2).\n   224\tfunc killPinnedChild(pid, parent int) (bool, error) {\n   225\t\tfd, err := unix.PidfdOpen(pid, 0)\n   226\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   227\t\t\treturn false, nil\n   228\t\t}\n   229\t\tif err != nil {\n   230\t\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be pinned: %w\", pid, err)\n   231\t\t}\n   232\t\tdefer unix.Close(fd)\n   233\t\tst, err := readShimProcStat(pid)\n   234\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && (st.ppid != parent || st.zombie) {\n   235\t\t\treturn false, nil\n   236\t\t}\n   237\t\tif err != nil {\n   238\t\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err)\n   239\t\t}\n   240\t\tif err := unix.PidfdSendSignal(fd, unix.SIGKILL, nil, 0); err != nil {\n   241\t\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   242\t\t\t\treturn false, nil\n   243\t\t\t}\n   244\t\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be ended: %w\", pid, err)\n   245\t\t}\n   246\t\treturn true, nil\n   247\t}\n   248\t\n   249\t// parseReviewShimReport reads the report the shim wrote to its pipe.\n   250\tfunc parseReviewShimReport(raw []byte) (reviewShimReport, error) {\n   251\t\tvar r reviewShimReport\n   252\t\tif len(raw) == 0 {\n   253\t\t\treturn r, fmt.Errorf(\"the review shim left no report\")\n   254\t\t}\n   255\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &r); err != nil {\n   256\t\t\treturn r, fmt.Errorf(\"the review shim report is unreadable: %w\", err)\n   257\t\t}\n   258\t\treturn r, nil\n   259\t}\n--- process reaper ---\n     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\t// Leftover reviewer processes, the fallback of an embedder that does not run\n     6\t// the adapter under the review run shim (review_shim.go), which is the Linux\n     7\t// path of the pose command (spec\n     8\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1, L6): an adapter such as\n     9\t// `codex exec` runs each command in a session of its own, so killing the\n    10\t// adapter's process group misses a command the reviewer left running, and\n    11\t// that command keeps writing into the run's runtime directory while the\n    12\t// cleanup inventory reads it. Every process of the run inherits\n    13\t// SealedCheckoutEnv naming the run's checkout, so the dispatch finds them by\n    14\t// that entry, ends them and waits for them before the inventory.\n    15\t//\n    16\t// Each process is pinned by a pidfd before it is signalled, and its\n    17\t// environment is read again through the pinned process, so a pid reused by\n    18\t// an unrelated process between the scan and the signal is never killed\n    19\t// (review round 1, N3). A scan that cannot list or read the state of the\n    20\t// processes fails. A process of this user whose environment cannot be read\n    21\t// (one that made itself non-inspectable) cannot be matched: one that already\n    22\t// existed before the adapter started is not the run's and is skipped; any\n    23\t// other may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable\n    24\t// (review round 2, N2).\n    25\t\n    26\timport (\n    27\t\t\"bytes\"\n    28\t\t\"errors\"\n    29\t\t\"fmt\"\n    30\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    31\t\t\"os\"\n    32\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    33\t\t\"strconv\"\n    34\t\t\"strings\"\n    35\t\t\"syscall\"\n    36\t\t\"time\"\n    37\t\n    38\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    39\t)\n    40\t\n    41\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses ends every process whose environment names\n    42\t// worktree as its sealed checkout and returns a description of each. An\n    43\t// error means the run's processes could not be proven ended within the bound.\n    44\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree string, baseline map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) {\n    45\t\tif worktree == \"\" {\n    46\t\t\treturn nil, 0, nil\n    47\t\t}\n    48\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\" + worktree)\n    49\t\tvar reaped []string\n    50\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n    51\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n    52\t\tunreadable := 0\n    53\t\tfor {\n    54\t\t\talive, opaque, err := reviewMarkedProcesses(entry)\n    55\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    56\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    57\t\t\t}\n    58\t\t\tunreadable = 0\n    59\t\t\tfor pid, start := range opaque {\n    60\t\t\t\tif prior, ok := baseline[pid]; !ok || prior != start {\n    61\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d of this user started during the run and cannot be inspected; it may be the run's and was not ended\", pid)\n    62\t\t\t\t}\n    63\t\t\t\tunreadable++\n    64\t\t\t}\n    65\t\t\tfor _, pid := range alive {\n    66\t\t\t\tif !seen[pid] {\n    67\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n    68\t\t\t\t\t// Only the pid: the name is the reviewer's to choose and is not\n    69\t\t\t\t\t// recorded (review round 7, N4).\n    70\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, strconv.Itoa(pid))\n    71\t\t\t\t}\n    72\t\t\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid, entry); err != nil {\n    73\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    74\t\t\t\t}\n    75\t\t\t}\n    76\t\t\tif len(alive) == 0 {\n    77\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, nil\n    78\t\t\t}\n    79\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    80\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended\", len(alive))\n    81\t\t\t}\n    82\t\t\ttime.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)\n    83\t\t}\n    84\t}\n    85\t\n    86\t// reviewMarkedProcesses lists the live processes whose environment holds\n    87\t// entry, and counts this user's processes whose environment could not be\n    88\t// read. A process that is gone is skipped.\n    89\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte) ([]int, map[int]string, error) {\n    90\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    91\t\tif err != nil {\n    92\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    93\t\t}\n    94\t\tunreadable := map[int]string{}\n    95\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    96\t\tvar out []int\n    97\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    98\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n    99\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n   100\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   101\t\t\t}\n   102\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   103\t\t\tswitch {\n   104\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n   105\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   106\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n   107\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n   108\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n   109\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   110\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   111\t\t\t\t}\n   112\t\t\t\tstart, serr := processStartTime(pid)\n   113\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(serr) {\n   114\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   115\t\t\t\t}\n   116\t\t\t\tif serr != nil || start == \"\" {\n   117\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d start could not be read: %v\", pid, serr)\n   118\t\t\t\t}\n   119\t\t\t\tunreadable[pid] = start\n   120\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   121\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   122\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   123\t\t\t}\n   124\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   125\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   126\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   127\t\t\t}\n   128\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   129\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   130\t\t\t}\n   131\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   132\t\t}\n   133\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n   134\t}\n   135\t\n   136\t// killPinnedMarkedProcess signals pid only through a pidfd opened on it,\n   137\t// after the environment read through that same pinned process still holds\n   138\t// entry.\n   139\tfunc killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid int, entry []byte) error {\n   140\t\tfd, err := unix.PidfdOpen(pid, 0)\n   141\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   142\t\t\treturn nil\n   143\t\t}\n   144\t\tif err != nil {\n   145\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be pinned: %w\", pid, err)\n   146\t\t}\n   147\t\tdefer unix.Close(fd)\n   148\t\t// The pidfd names one process for its lifetime; if pid was reused before\n   149\t\t// it was opened, the new process does not carry this run's entry.\n   150\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   151\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && !marked {\n   152\t\t\treturn nil\n   153\t\t}\n   154\t\tif err != nil {\n   155\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err)\n   156\t\t}\n   157\t\tif err := unix.PidfdSendSignal(fd, unix.SIGKILL, nil, 0); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   158\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be ended: %w\", pid, err)\n   159\t\t}\n   160\t\treturn nil\n   161\t}\n   162\t\n   163\tfunc reviewProcessMarked(pid int, entry []byte) (bool, error) {\n   164\t\tenviron, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"environ\"))\n   165\t\tif err != nil {\n   166\t\t\treturn false, err\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\tfor _, kv := range bytes.Split(environ, []byte{0}) {\n   169\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(kv, entry) {\n   170\t\t\t\treturn true, nil\n   171\t\t\t}\n   172\t\t}\n   173\t\treturn false, nil\n   174\t}\n   175\t\n   176\tfunc reviewProcessOwner(pid int) (int, error) {\n   177\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid)))\n   178\t\tif err != nil {\n   179\t\t\treturn 0, err\n   180\t\t}\n   181\t\tst, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n   182\t\tif !ok {\n   183\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d owner unavailable\", pid)\n   184\t\t}\n   185\t\treturn int(st.Uid), nil\n   186\t}\n   187\t\n   188\tfunc reviewProcessGoneErr(err error) bool {\n   189\t\treturn errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) || errors.Is(err, syscall.ESRCH)\n   190\t}\n   191\t\n   192\tfunc reviewProcessName(pid int) string {\n   193\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"comm\"))\n   194\t\tif err != nil {\n   195\t\t\treturn \"?\"\n   196\t\t}\n   197\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(raw))\n   198\t}\n   199\t\n   200\tfunc reviewProcessZombie(pid int) (bool, error) {\n   201\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"stat\"))\n   202\t\tif err != nil {\n   203\t\t\treturn false, err\n   204\t\t}\n   205\t\t// The state follows the parenthesised command name.\n   206\t\tif i := bytes.LastIndexByte(raw, ')'); i >= 0 && i+2 < len(raw) {\n   207\t\t\treturn raw[i+2] == 'Z', nil\n   208\t\t}\n   209\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state is unreadable\", pid)\n   210\t}\n   211\t\n   212\t// reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline records, before the adapter starts, the\n   213\t// processes of this user whose environment cannot be read, by pid and start\n   214\t// time: they cannot be the run's.\n   215\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string {\n   216\t\t_, opaque, _ := reviewMarkedProcesses([]byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\\x00\"))\n   217\t\treturn opaque\n   218\t}\n     1\t//go:build !linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport \"os/exec\"\n     6\t\n     7\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses has no portable way to read another process's\n     8\t// environment; outside Linux the process-group kill is the only termination.\n     9\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(string, map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) { return nil, 0, nil }\n    10\t\n    11\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string { return nil }\n    12\t\n    13\t// RunReviewShim is the Linux review run shim; elsewhere it is not used.\n    14\tfunc RunReviewShim(args []string) int { return 125 }\n    15\t\n    16\tfunc parseReviewShimReport([]byte) (reviewShimReport, error) { return reviewShimReport{}, nil }\n    17\t\n    18\tfunc stopReviewShim(cmd *exec.Cmd) func() error { return cmd.Cancel }\n--- adapter containment ---\n     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// The trusted-process backend bounds engine capture, not the adapter's address\n     4\t// space or filesystem. Capabilities describe enforcement, never configuration.\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"bytes\"\n     7\t\t\"context\"\n     8\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     9\t\t\"errors\"\n    10\t\t\"fmt\"\n    11\t\t\"io\"\n    12\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    13\t\t\"os\"\n    14\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    15\t\t\"regexp\"\n    16\t\t\"runtime\"\n    17\t\t\"sort\"\n    18\t\t\"strings\"\n    19\t\t\"sync\"\n    20\t\t\"time\"\n    21\t\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n    22\t)\n    23\t\n    24\tconst ReviewNotesMaxBytes = 16 << 10\n    25\t\n    26\t// ReviewerContainment is optional schema-1 adapter policy. Pointers distinguish\n    27\t// omitted finite defaults from explicit zero, which is invalid for byte limits.\n    28\ttype ReviewerContainment struct {\n    29\t\tSchemaVersion       int      `json:\"schema_version\"`\n    30\t\tProfile             string   `json:\"profile\"`\n    31\t\tRequired            []string `json:\"required,omitempty\"`\n    32\t\tEnvironment         []string `json:\"environment,omitempty\"`\n    33\t\tCredentials         []string `json:\"credentials,omitempty\"`\n    34\t\tStreamBytes         *int64   `json:\"stream_bytes,omitempty\"`\n    35\t\tOutputBytes         *int64   `json:\"output_bytes,omitempty\"`\n    36\t\tRetainedBytes       *int64   `json:\"retained_bytes,omitempty\"`\n    37\t\tRetentionTTLSeconds int64    `json:\"retention_ttl_seconds\"`\n    38\t\tMemoryBytes         *int64   `json:\"memory_bytes,omitempty\"`\n    39\t\tCPUTimeMS           *int64   `json:\"cpu_time_ms,omitempty\"`\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\t// UnmarshalJSON refuses misspelled enforcement fields instead of dropping them.\n    43\tfunc (p *ReviewerContainment) UnmarshalJSON(raw []byte) error {\n    44\t\tvar fields map[string]json.RawMessage\n    45\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &fields); err != nil {\n    46\t\t\treturn err\n    47\t\t}\n    48\t\tfor name, value := range fields {\n    49\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(bytes.TrimSpace(value), []byte(\"null\")) {\n    50\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"containment field %s cannot be null; omit optional fields for defaults\", name)\n    51\t\t\t}\n    52\t\t}\n    53\t\ttype plain ReviewerContainment\n    54\t\tvar decoded plain\n    55\t\td := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n    56\t\td.DisallowUnknownFields()\n    57\t\tif err := d.Decode(&decoded); err != nil {\n    58\t\t\treturn err\n    59\t\t}\n    60\t\t*p = ReviewerContainment(decoded)\n    61\t\treturn nil\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\t// ReviewExecutionSafety is retained with the exact run and covered by its hash,\n    65\t// witness and optional native signature. No environment values are exported.\n    66\ttype ReviewExecutionSafety struct {\n    67\t\tSchemaVersion   int               `json:\"schema_version\"`\n    68\t\tProfile         string            `json:\"profile\"`\n    69\t\tPlatform        string            `json:\"platform\"`\n    70\t\tCapabilities    map[string]string `json:\"capabilities\"`\n    71\t\tLimitations     []string          `json:\"limitations\"`\n    72\t\tStreamBytes     int64             `json:\"stream_bytes\"`\n    73\t\tOutputBytes     int64             `json:\"output_bytes\"`\n    74\t\tRetainedBytes   int64             `json:\"retained_bytes\"`\n    75\t\tTimeoutMS       int64             `json:\"timeout_ms\"`\n    76\t\tMaxRuns         int               `json:\"max_runs_per_bundle\"`\n    77\t\tRetention       string            `json:\"retention\"`\n    78\t\tCaptureComplete bool              `json:\"capture_complete\"`\n    79\t\tRuntimeID       string            `json:\"runtime_id,omitempty\"`\n    80\t\tExecutionCause  string            `json:\"execution_cause,omitempty\"`\n    81\t\tOperation       OperationResult   `json:\"operation\"`\n    82\t}\n    83\t\n    84\tvar adapterEnvironmentName = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$`)\n    85\t\n    86\tfunc effectiveReviewMaxRuns(a ReviewerAdapter) int {\n    87\t\tif a.MaxRunsPerBundle == 0 {\n    88\t\t\treturn 3\n    89\t\t}\n    90\t\treturn a.MaxRunsPerBundle\n    91\t}\n    92\t\n    93\t// ResolveReviewerContainment is shared by preview, execution and consumers.\n    94\t// It makes no changes, including attempt reservations.\n    95\tfunc ResolveReviewerContainment(a ReviewerAdapter) (*ReviewExecutionSafety, error) {\n    96\t\tsafety, err := resolveReviewerContainment(a)\n    97\t\treturn safety, refusal(DelegationReasonContainment, err)\n    98\t}\n    99\t\n   100\tfunc resolveReviewerContainment(a ReviewerAdapter) (*ReviewExecutionSafety, error) {\n   101\t\tfor _, identity := range []string{a.Vendor, a.Model} {\n   102\t\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(identity) == \"\" || strings.ContainsAny(identity, \"\\x00\\r\\n\") {\n   103\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter identity must be nonempty without surrounding whitespace\")\n   104\t\t\t}\n   105\t\t}\n   106\t\tif len(a.Command) == 0 || strings.TrimSpace(a.Command[0]) == \"\" || strings.TrimSpace(a.Command[0]) != a.Command[0] {\n   107\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter argv requires a nonempty executable\")\n   108\t\t}\n   109\t\tfor _, arg := range a.Command {\n   110\t\t\tif strings.ContainsRune(arg, 0) {\n   111\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter argv contains NUL\")\n   112\t\t\t}\n   113\t\t}\n   114\t\tif a.Executor != \"\" && (strings.TrimSpace(a.Executor) != a.Executor || !strings.HasPrefix(a.Executor, \"agent:\") || strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimPrefix(a.Executor, \"agent:\")) == \"\") {\n   115\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter executor identity is invalid\")\n   116\t\t}\n   117\t\tif a.MaxRunsPerBundle < 0 || a.MaxRunsPerBundle > 100 {\n   118\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"max_runs_per_bundle must be 1..100 when present (omitted defaults to 3)\")\n   119\t\t}\n   120\t\ttimeout := time.Hour\n   121\t\tif a.Timeout != \"\" {\n   122\t\t\tvar err error\n   123\t\t\ttimeout, err = time.ParseDuration(a.Timeout)\n   124\t\t\tif err != nil || timeout < time.Millisecond || timeout > 24*time.Hour || strings.TrimSpace(a.Timeout) != a.Timeout {\n   125\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter timeout must be a positive duration up to 24h\")\n   126\t\t\t}\n   127\t\t}\n   128\t\tr := &ReviewExecutionSafety{SchemaVersion: 1, Profile: \"legacy-trusted\", Platform: runtime.GOOS + \"/\" + runtime.GOARCH, StreamBytes: 8 << 20, OutputBytes: 64 << 10, RetainedBytes: 16 << 20, TimeoutMS: timeout.Milliseconds(), MaxRuns: effectiveReviewMaxRuns(a), Retention: \"retain-evidence; ttl=0; no automatic deletion\", Capabilities: map[string]string{\n   129\t\t\t\"bounded-capture\": \"available\", \"environment-allowlist\": \"available\", \"parent-termination\": \"available\", \"process-group-termination\": \"unsupported\", \"filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\", \"origin-isolation\": \"unavailable\", \"shared-git-isolation\": \"unavailable\", \"network-isolation\": \"unavailable\", \"credential-filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\", \"escaped-descendant-termination\": \"unavailable\", \"memory-limit\": \"unavailable\", \"cpu-limit\": \"unavailable\", \"automatic-expiry\": \"unavailable\",\n   130\t\t}, Limitations: []string{\"trusted local executable required; worktree is not a sandbox\", \"outside writes, transient writes, shared Git and credential files are not isolated\", \"no memory/CPU quota or control of descendants escaping the process group\", \"cleanup filesystem calls remain subject to operating-system I/O latency\"}}\n   131\t\tif runtime.GOOS == \"linux\" {\n   132\t\t\tif err := reviewProcessGroupAvailable(); err == nil {\n   133\t\t\t\tr.Capabilities[\"process-group-termination\"] = \"available\"\n   134\t\t\t\t// A descendant that left the group is still ended while its\n   135\t\t\t\t// environment keeps the run's sealed-checkout entry; one that\n   136\t\t\t\t// clears it is not, so the guarantee is not \"available\" (spec\n   137\t\t\t\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1, L1).\n   138\t\t\t\tr.Capabilities[\"escaped-descendant-termination\"] = \"environment-marked\"\n   139\t\t\t\tfor i, limit := range r.Limitations {\n   140\t\t\t\t\tif limit == \"no memory/CPU quota or control of descendants escaping the process group\" {\n   141\t\t\t\t\t\tr.Limitations[i] = \"no memory/CPU quota; descendants escaping the process group are ended only while they keep the run's sealed-checkout environment entry\"\n   142\t\t\t\t\t}\n   143\t\t\t\t}\n   144\t\t\t} else {\n   145\t\t\t\tr.Capabilities[\"process-group-termination\"] = \"unavailable\"\n   146\t\t\t\tr.Limitations = append(r.Limitations, \"process inventory not observable on this host\")\n   147\t\t\t}\n   148\t\t} else {\n   149\t\t\tr.Limitations = append(r.Limitations, \"process-group termination not qualified on this platform\")\n   150\t\t\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n   151\t\t\t\t// On Windows the dispatch does not end the adapter's descendants\n   152\t\t\t\t// at all (review round 12, N1).\n   153\t\t\t\tr.Limitations = append(r.Limitations, \"the adapter's descendants are not ended on Windows: a process the reviewer leaves running survives the run\")\n   154\t\t\t}\n   155\t\t}\n   156\t\tp := a.Containment\n   157\t\tif p == nil {\n   158\t\t\tr.Limitations = append(r.Limitations, \"legacy compatibility: HOME retained; other ambient credentials excluded\")\n   159\t\t\treturn r, nil\n   160\t\t}\n   161\t\tif p.SchemaVersion != 1 || p.Profile != \"trusted-process\" {\n   162\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported containment schema/profile; use schema_version 1 and trusted-process\")\n   163\t\t}\n   164\t\tr.Profile = p.Profile\n   165\t\tfor _, limit := range []struct {\n   166\t\t\tname   string\n   167\t\t\tvalue  *int64\n   168\t\t\ttarget *int64\n   169\t\t\tmax    int64\n   170\t\t}{{\"stream_bytes\", p.StreamBytes, &r.StreamBytes, 64 << 20}, {\"output_bytes\", p.OutputBytes, &r.OutputBytes, 128 << 10}, {\"retained_bytes\", p.RetainedBytes, &r.RetainedBytes, 128 << 20}} {\n   171\t\t\tif limit.value != nil {\n   172\t\t\t\tif *limit.value <= 0 || *limit.value > limit.max {\n   173\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%s must be 1..%d bytes\", limit.name, limit.max)\n   174\t\t\t\t}\n   175\t\t\t\t*limit.target = *limit.value\n   176\t\t\t}\n   177\t\t}\n   178\t\tif r.RetainedBytes < r.StreamBytes+6*r.OutputBytes+(1<<20) {\n   179\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"retained_bytes must cover stream_bytes + 6*output_bytes + 1048576 bytes of record overhead\")\n   180\t\t}\n   181\t\tif p.RetentionTTLSeconds != 0 {\n   182\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"automatic retention expiry unavailable; retention_ttl_seconds must be 0 (retain evidence)\")\n   183\t\t}\n   184\t\tif p.MemoryBytes != nil || p.CPUTimeMS != nil {\n   185\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"memory/CPU enforcement unavailable in trusted-process; omit memory_bytes/cpu_time_ms\")\n   186\t\t}\n   187\t\tfor _, capability := range p.Required {\n   188\t\t\tstate, ok := r.Capabilities[capability]\n   189\t\t\tif !ok || state != \"available\" {\n   190\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"required capability %q unsupported/unavailable on %s; select a qualified backend or remove that requirement\", capability, r.Platform)\n   191\t\t\t}\n   192\t\t}\n   193\t\tif len(p.Environment) > 128 || len(p.Credentials) > 32 {\n   194\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"environment allowlist exceeds 128 names or 32 credential names\")\n   195\t\t}\n   196\t\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n   197\t\tfor _, name := range append(append([]string{}, p.Environment...), p.Credentials...) {\n   198\t\t\tif len(name) > 128 || !adapterEnvironmentName.MatchString(name) || seen[strings.ToUpper(name)] {\n   199\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"environment/credentials require unique valid variable names\")\n   200\t\t\t}\n   201\t\t\tupper := strings.ToUpper(name)\n   202\t\t\tseen[upper] = true\n   203\t\t\t// Loader hooks can turn a trusted binary into an unrelated executable.\n   204\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(upper, \"LD_\") || strings.HasPrefix(upper, \"DYLD_\") || strings.HasPrefix(upper, \"GIT_\") || upper == \"BASH_ENV\" || upper == \"ENV\" || upper == \"SHELLOPTS\" || upper == \"HOME\" || upper == \"USERPROFILE\" || upper == \"TMPDIR\" || upper == \"TMP\" || upper == \"TEMP\" {\n   205\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"environment variable %s is reserved or unsafe\", name)\n   206\t\t\t}\n   207\t\t}\n   208\t\tfor _, name := range p.Environment {\n   209\t\t\tupper := strings.ToUpper(name)\n   210\t\t\tfor _, mark := range []string{\"TOKEN\", \"SECRET\", \"PASSWORD\", \"CREDENTIAL\", \"API_KEY\", \"PRIVATE_KEY\"} {\n   211\t\t\t\tif strings.Contains(upper, mark) {\n   212\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"sensitive environment variable %s requires credentials authorization\", name)\n   213\t\t\t\t}\n   214\t\t\t}\n   215\t\t}\n   216\t\treturn r, nil\n   217\t}\n   218\t\n   219\tfunc validateExplicitReviewBudget(raw []byte) error {\n   220\t\tvar policy struct {\n   221\t\t\tAdapters map[string]map[string]json.RawMessage `json:\"adapters\"`\n   222\t\t}\n   223\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &policy); err != nil {\n   224\t\t\treturn err\n   225\t\t}\n   226\t\tfor name, a := range policy.Adapters {\n   227\t\t\tif value, ok := a[\"max_runs_per_bundle\"]; ok {\n   228\t\t\t\tvar n int\n   229\t\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(bytes.TrimSpace(value), []byte(\"null\")) || json.Unmarshal(value, &n) != nil || n <= 0 || n > 100 {\n   230\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"adapter %s: explicit max_runs_per_bundle must be 1..100; omit for default 3\", name)\n   231\t\t\t\t}\n   232\t\t\t}\n   233\t\t}\n   234\t\treturn nil\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\tfunc reviewAdapterEnvironment(a ReviewerAdapter, tmp, brief, notes string) ([]string, []string, error) {\n   238\t\tnames := []string{\"PATH\", \"LANG\", \"LC_ALL\", \"LC_CTYPE\", \"SYSTEMROOT\", \"WINDIR\"}\n   239\t\tif a.Containment == nil {\n   240\t\t\tnames = append(names, \"HOME\", \"USERPROFILE\")\n   241\t\t} else {\n   242\t\t\tnames = append(names, a.Containment.Environment...)\n   243\t\t}\n   244\t\tvalues := map[string]string{}\n   245\t\tput := func(name, value string) {\n   246\t\t\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n   247\t\t\t\tname = strings.ToUpper(name)\n   248\t\t\t}\n   249\t\t\tvalues[name] = value\n   250\t\t}\n   251\t\tfor _, name := range names {\n   252\t\t\tif value, ok := os.LookupEnv(name); ok {\n   253\t\t\t\tput(name, value)\n   254\t\t\t}\n   255\t\t}\n   256\t\tsecrets := []string{}\n   257\t\tif a.Containment != nil {\n   258\t\t\tfor _, name := range a.Containment.Credentials {\n   259\t\t\t\tif value, ok := os.LookupEnv(name); ok && value != \"\" {\n   260\t\t\t\t\tif len(value) < 8 || len(value) > 64<<10 {\n   261\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"authorized credential value has unsupported length\")\n   262\t\t\t\t\t}\n   263\t\t\t\t\tif strings.Contains(brief, value) || strings.Contains(notes, value) {\n   264\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"brief/notes contain an authorized credential; refusing execution\")\n   265\t\t\t\t\t}\n   266\t\t\t\t\tput(name, value)\n   267\t\t\t\t\tsecrets = append(secrets, value)\n   268\t\t\t\t}\n   269\t\t\t}\n   270\t\t\tvalues[\"HOME\"] = tmp\n   271\t\t\tvalues[\"USERPROFILE\"] = tmp\n   272\t\t}\n   273\t\tvalues[\"TMPDIR\"] = tmp\n   274\t\tvalues[\"TMP\"] = tmp\n   275\t\tvalues[\"TEMP\"] = tmp\n   276\t\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(values))\n   277\t\tfor k := range values {\n   278\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, k)\n   279\t\t}\n   280\t\tsort.Strings(keys)\n   281\t\tenv := make([]string, 0, len(keys))\n   282\t\tfor _, k := range keys {\n   283\t\t\tenv = append(env, k+\"=\"+values[k])\n   284\t\t}\n   285\t\t// Replace overlapping credentials longest first so no residual suffix leaks.\n   286\t\tsort.Slice(secrets, func(i, j int) bool { return len(secrets[i]) > len(secrets[j]) })\n   287\t\treturn env, secrets, nil\n   288\t}\n   289\t\n   290\t// A single longest-first replacement pass handles overlapping session and\n   291\t// credential values without rescanning placeholders. The writer refuses growth\n   292\t// beyond the byte budget even for a one-byte session repeated across a stream.\n   293\tfunc redactReviewCapture(raw []byte, secrets []string, session string, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n   294\t\treplacements := map[string]string{}\n   295\t\tfor _, secret := range secrets {\n   296\t\t\treplacements[secret] = \"[credential]\"\n   297\t\t}\n   298\t\tif session != \"\" {\n   299\t\t\tif _, exists := replacements[session]; !exists {\n   300\t\t\t\treplacements[session] = \"[private-session]\"\n   301\t\t\t}\n   302\t\t}\n   303\t\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(replacements))\n   304\t\tfor key := range replacements {\n   305\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n   306\t\t}\n   307\t\tsort.Slice(keys, func(i, j int) bool {\n   308\t\t\tif len(keys[i]) == len(keys[j]) {\n   309\t\t\t\treturn keys[i] < keys[j]\n   310\t\t\t}\n   311\t\t\treturn len(keys[i]) > len(keys[j])\n   312\t\t})\n   313\t\tpairs := make([]string, 0, len(keys)*2)\n   314\t\tfor _, key := range keys {\n   315\t\t\tpairs = append(pairs, key, replacements[key])\n   316\t\t}\n   317\t\tw := &reviewRedactionWriter{limit: limit}\n   318\t\tif _, err := strings.NewReplacer(pairs...).WriteString(w, string(raw)); err != nil {\n   319\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   320\t\t}\n   321\t\treturn w.buf.Bytes(), nil\n   322\t}\n   323\t\n   324\ttype reviewRedactionWriter struct {\n   325\t\tbuf   bytes.Buffer\n   326\t\tlimit int64\n   327\t}\n   328\t\n   329\tfunc (w *reviewRedactionWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\n   330\t\tif int64(w.buf.Len())+int64(len(p)) > w.limit {\n   331\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"redacted capture exceeds byte budget\")\n   332\t\t}\n   333\t\treturn w.buf.Write(p)\n   334\t}\n   335\t\n   336\t// Shared writer bounds concurrent stdout/stderr as one budget. Cancellation is\n   337\t// triggered on the first excess byte; subsequent writes do not grow storage.\n   338\ttype reviewBoundedCapture struct {\n   339\t\tmu       sync.Mutex\n   340\t\tbuf      bytes.Buffer\n   341\t\tlimit    int64\n   342\t\toverflow bool\n   343\t\tcancel   context.CancelFunc\n   344\t}\n   345\t\n   346\tfunc (w *reviewBoundedCapture) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\n   347\t\tw.mu.Lock()\n   348\t\tdefer w.mu.Unlock()\n   349\t\tn := len(p)\n   350\t\tremaining := w.limit - int64(w.buf.Len())\n   351\t\tif int64(n) > remaining {\n   352\t\t\tw.buf.Write(p[:int(remaining)])\n   353\t\t\tw.overflow = true\n   354\t\t\tif w.cancel != nil {\n   355\t\t\t\tw.cancel()\n   356\t\t\t}\n   357\t\t} else {\n   358\t\t\tw.buf.Write(p)\n   359\t\t}\n   360\t\treturn n, nil\n   361\t}\n   362\tfunc (w *reviewBoundedCapture) result() ([]byte, bool) {\n   363\t\tw.mu.Lock()\n   364\t\tdefer w.mu.Unlock()\n   365\t\treturn append([]byte(nil), w.buf.Bytes()...), w.overflow\n   366\t}\n   367\t\n   368\t// ReadReviewAdapterFile refuses links/special files before opening; the platform\n   369\t// opener also uses nonblocking/no-follow semantics where available.\n   370\tfunc ReadReviewAdapterFile(path string, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n   371\t\tbefore, err := os.Lstat(path)\n   372\t\tif err != nil {\n   373\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   374\t\t}\n   375\t\tif !before.Mode().IsRegular() || before.Size() > limit {\n   376\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter file must be regular, non-symlink and at most %d bytes\", limit)\n   377\t\t}\n   378\t\tf, err := openReviewAdapterFile(path)\n   379\t\tif err != nil {\n   380\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   381\t\t}\n   382\t\tdefer f.Close()\n   383\t\tafter, err := f.Stat()\n   384\t\tif err != nil {\n   385\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   386\t\t}\n   387\t\tif !after.Mode().IsRegular() || !os.SameFile(before, after) {\n   388\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter file changed identity\")\n   389\t\t}\n   390\t\traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(f, limit+1))\n   391\t\tif err != nil {\n   392\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   393\t\t}\n   394\t\tif int64(len(raw)) > limit {\n   395\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter file exceeds %d bytes\", limit)\n   396\t\t}\n   397\t\tlast, err := os.Lstat(path)\n   398\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(after, last) || last.Size() != int64(len(raw)) {\n   399\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"adapter file changed while reading\")\n   400\t\t}\n   401\t\treturn raw, nil\n   402\t}\n   403\t\n   404\tfunc readReviewAdapterOutput(root *os.Root, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n   405\t\treturn readReviewRootFile(root, \"output.txt\", limit)\n   406\t}\n   407\tfunc readReviewRootFile(root *os.Root, path string, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n   408\t\tbefore, err := root.Lstat(path)\n   409\t\tif err != nil {\n   410\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   411\t\t}\n   412\t\tif !before.Mode().IsRegular() || before.Size() > limit {\n   413\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unsafe or oversized output file\")\n   414\t\t}\n   415\t\tf, err := openReviewRootFile(root, path)\n   416\t\tif err != nil {\n   417\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   418\t\t}\n   419\t\tdefer f.Close()\n   420\t\tafter, err := f.Stat()\n   421\t\tif err != nil {\n   422\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   423\t\t}\n   424\t\tif !after.Mode().IsRegular() || !os.SameFile(before, after) {\n   425\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"output identity changed\")\n   426\t\t}\n   427\t\traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(f, limit+1))\n   428\t\tif err != nil {\n   429\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   430\t\t}\n   431\t\tif int64(len(raw)) > limit {\n   432\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"output exceeds byte budget\")\n   433\t\t}\n   434\t\tlast, err := root.Lstat(path)\n   435\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(last, after) || last.Size() != int64(len(raw)) {\n   436\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"output changed while reading\")\n   437\t\t}\n   438\t\treturn raw, nil\n   439\t}\n   440\t\n   441\tfunc validateReviewNotes(notes string) error {\n   442\t\tif len(notes) > ReviewNotesMaxBytes || !utf8.ValidString(notes) || strings.ContainsRune(notes, 0) {\n   443\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"review notes must be valid UTF-8, without NUL, at most %d bytes\", ReviewNotesMaxBytes)\n   444\t\t}\n   445\t\treturn nil\n   446\t}\n   447\t\n   448\t// reviewCleanupOwnership holds descriptors opened before the adapter starts.\n   449\t// Git's recursive worktree-remove command takes a path, so it cannot safely\n   450\t// delete after a hostile rename. Workspace and exact registration are instead\n   451\t// removed independently through confined roots. No global prune is performed.\n   452\ttype reviewCleanupOwnership struct {\n   453\t\tremoved          bool\n   454\t\truntime          *os.Root\n   455\t\tregistry         *os.Root\n   456\t\tregistration     string\n   457\t\tregistrationInfo os.FileInfo\n   458\t\tbacklink         string\n   459\t\t// inventoryBytes bounds the bytes the worktree's cleanup may remove: the\n   460\t\t// checked-out commit's tree plus the snapshot margin, read from the\n   461\t\t// coordinator repository when the worktree is registered (spec\n   462\t\t// pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree).\n   463\t\tinventoryBytes       int64\n   464\t\tgitlinkMetadata      os.FileInfo\n   465\t\tgitlinkMetadataBytes int64\n   466\t}\n   467\t\n   468\tfunc (s Store) captureReviewCleanupOwnership(runtime *os.Root, worktree string, marker []byte) (*reviewCleanupOwnership, error) {\n   469\t\traw, err := snapshotGit(s.Root, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-common-dir\")\n   470\t\tif err != nil {\n   471\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   472\t\t}\n   473\t\tparent := filepath.Join(strings.TrimSpace(string(raw)), \"worktrees\")\n   474\t\tpath := strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimPrefix(string(marker), \"gitdir: \"))\n   475\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(string(marker), \"gitdir: \") || !filepath.IsAbs(path) || filepath.Dir(path) != parent {\n   476\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unexpected worktree registration\")\n   477\t\t}\n   478\t\tregistry, err := os.OpenRoot(parent)\n   479\t\tif err != nil {\n   480\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   481\t\t}\n   482\t\tname := filepath.Base(path)\n   483\t\tinfo, err := registry.Lstat(name)\n   484\t\tif err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n   485\t\t\tregistry.Close()\n   486\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration unavailable\")\n   487\t\t}\n   488\t\to := &reviewCleanupOwnership{runtime: runtime, registry: registry, registration: name, registrationInfo: info, backlink: filepath.Join(worktree, \".git\"), inventoryBytes: gitSnapshotMarginBytes}\n   489\t\tif head, err := registry.ReadFile(filepath.Join(name, \"HEAD\")); err == nil {\n   490\t\t\tif commit := strings.TrimSpace(string(head)); !strings.HasPrefix(commit, \"ref:\") && commit != \"\" {\n   491\t\t\t\tif listing, err := listCommittedTree(s.Root, commit); err == nil {\n   492\t\t\t\t\to.inventoryBytes = gitSnapshotBudget(gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing))\n   493\t\t\t\t}\n   494\t\t\t}\n   495\t\t}\n   496\t\tchild, err := registry.OpenRoot(name)\n   497\t\tif err != nil {\n   498\t\t\tregistry.Close()\n   499\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   500\t\t}\n   501\t\tbacklink, err := readReviewRootFile(child, \"gitdir\", 4096)\n   502\t\tchild.Close()\n   503\t\tif err != nil || strings.TrimSpace(string(backlink)) != o.backlink {\n   504\t\t\tregistry.Close()\n   505\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration backlink differs\")\n   506\t\t}\n   507\t\treturn o, nil\n   508\t}\n   509\t\n   510\tfunc (s Store) cleanupReviewResources(tmp string, owned os.FileInfo, worktree string, worktreeOwned os.FileInfo, gitMarker []byte, ownership ...*reviewCleanupOwnership) error {\n   511\t\tvar o *reviewCleanupOwnership\n   512\t\tif len(ownership) > 0 {\n   513\t\t\to = ownership[0]\n   514\t\t}\n   515\t\tcurrent, err := os.Lstat(tmp)\n   516\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   517\t\t\tif (o != nil && !o.removed) || (o == nil && worktreeOwned != nil) {\n   518\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime path disappeared without confirmed cleanup; resources may remain\")\n   519\t\t\t}\n   520\t\t\treturn nil\n   521\t\t}\n   522\t\tif err != nil || !current.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(owned, current) {\n   523\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup refused: runtime directory identity changed\")\n   524\t\t}\n   525\t\n   526\t\tvar root *os.Root\n   527\t\tif o != nil {\n   528\t\t\troot = o.runtime\n   529\t\t} else {\n   530\t\t\troot, err = os.OpenRoot(tmp)\n   531\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   532\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup root unavailable\")\n   533\t\t\t}\n   534\t\t\tdefer root.Close()\n   535\t\t}\n   536\t\tstat, err := root.Stat(\".\")\n   537\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, stat) {\n   538\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup root identity changed\")\n   539\t\t}\n   540\t\tif worktreeOwned != nil {\n   541\t\t\tinfo, err := root.Lstat(\"worktree\")\n   542\t\t\tif err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   543\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup unavailable\")\n   544\t\t\t}\n   545\t\t\tif err == nil {\n   546\t\t\t\tmarker, e := readReviewRootFile(root, \"worktree/.git\", 4096)\n   547\t\t\t\tif e != nil || !info.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(worktreeOwned, info) || !bytes.Equal(marker, gitMarker) {\n   548\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup refused: worktree identity changed\")\n   549\t\t\t\t}\n   550\t\t\t}\n   551\t\t\tif o == nil || o.registry == nil {\n   552\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration ownership unavailable; resources retained\")\n   553\t\t\t}\n   554\t\t\tinfo, e := o.registry.Lstat(o.registration)\n   555\t\t\tif e != nil || !info.IsDir() || !os.SameFile(info, o.registrationInfo) {\n   556\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration identity changed\")\n   557\t\t\t}\n   558\t\t\tregistration, e := o.registry.OpenRoot(o.registration)\n   559\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   560\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration unavailable\")\n   561\t\t\t}\n   562\t\t\tdefer registration.Close()\n   563\t\t\tinfo, e = registration.Stat(\".\")\n   564\t\t\tif e != nil || !os.SameFile(info, o.registrationInfo) {\n   565\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration identity changed\")\n   566\t\t\t}\n   567\t\t\tbacklink, e := readReviewRootFile(registration, \"gitdir\", 4096)\n   568\t\t\tif e != nil || strings.TrimSpace(string(backlink)) != o.backlink {\n   569\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup registration backlink changed\")\n   570\t\t\t}\n   571\t\t\tfor _, lock := range []string{\"locked\", \"index.lock\", \"HEAD.lock\"} {\n   572\t\t\t\tif _, e := registration.Lstat(lock); !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   573\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration has a live or unknown lock; resources retained\")\n   574\t\t\t\t}\n   575\t\t\t}\n   576\t\t\tif err == nil {\n   577\t\t\t\ttree, e := root.OpenRoot(\"worktree\")\n   578\t\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   579\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup root unavailable\")\n   580\t\t\t\t}\n   581\t\t\t\tinfo, e := tree.Stat(\".\")\n   582\t\t\t\tif e != nil || !os.SameFile(info, worktreeOwned) {\n   583\t\t\t\t\ttree.Close()\n   584\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup identity changed\")\n   585\t\t\t\t}\n   586\t\t\t\tlimit := gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n   587\t\t\t\tif o.inventoryBytes > limit {\n   588\t\t\t\t\tlimit = o.inventoryBytes\n   589\t\t\t\t}\n   590\t\t\t\te = removeReviewOwnedContents(tree, 100000, limit)\n   591\t\t\t\ttree.Close()\n   592\t\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   593\t\t\t\t\treturn e\n   594\t\t\t\t}\n   595\t\t\t\tif e := root.Remove(\"worktree\"); e != nil && !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   596\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup incomplete\")\n   597\t\t\t\t}\n   598\t\t\t}\n   599\t\t\tif e := removeReviewOwnedContents(registration, 1024, 256<<20); e != nil {\n   600\t\t\t\treturn e\n   601\t\t\t}\n   602\t\t\tregistration.Close()\n   603\t\t\tif e := o.registry.Remove(o.registration); e != nil && !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   604\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration cleanup incomplete\")\n   605\t\t\t}\n   606\t\t} else if _, e := root.Lstat(\"worktree\"); !errors.Is(e, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   607\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"partial worktree setup has no verified ownership; resources retained\")\n   608\t\t}\n   609\t\tif o != nil && o.gitlinkMetadata != nil {\n   610\t\t\tif err := removeReviewGitlinkMetadata(root, o.gitlinkMetadata, o.gitlinkMetadataBytes); err != nil {\n   611\t\t\t\treturn err\n   612\t\t\t}\n   613\t\t}\n   614\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers(root); err != nil {\n   615\t\t\treturn err\n   616\t\t}\n   617\t\tif err := removeReviewOwnedContents(root, reviewRuntimeMaxEntries, 128<<20); err != nil {\n   618\t\t\treturn err\n   619\t\t}\n   620\t\tcurrent, err = os.Lstat(tmp)\n   621\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, current) {\n   622\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime path changed during cleanup; replacement retained\")\n   623\t\t}\n   624\t\tif err := os.Remove(tmp); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   625\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime directory cleanup incomplete\")\n   626\t\t}\n   627\t\tif o != nil {\n   628\t\t\to.removed = true\n   629\t\t}\n   630\t\treturn nil\n   631\t}\n   632\t\n   633\t// Private gitlink stores are charged separately from the adapter's runtime\n   634\t// output. Both the opened directory and the removal target must be the\n   635\t// directory setup created inside the operation root.\n   636\tfunc removeReviewGitlinkMetadata(root *os.Root, owned os.FileInfo, limit int64) error {\n   637\t\tdir, err := root.OpenRoot(reviewGitlinkMetadataDir)\n   638\t\tif err != nil {\n   639\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"private gitlink metadata cleanup unavailable\")\n   640\t\t}\n   641\t\tdefer dir.Close()\n   642\t\tinfo, err := dir.Stat(\".\")\n   643\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, info) {\n   644\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"private gitlink metadata identity changed\")\n   645\t\t}\n   646\t\tif err := removeReviewOwnedContents(dir, 100000, limit); err != nil {\n   647\t\t\treturn err\n   648\t\t}\n   649\t\tinfo, err = root.Lstat(reviewGitlinkMetadataDir)\n   650\t\tif err != nil || !os.SameFile(owned, info) {\n   651\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"private gitlink metadata identity changed\")\n   652\t\t}\n   653\t\tdir.Close()\n   654\t\tif err := root.Remove(reviewGitlinkMetadataDir); err != nil {\n   655\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"private gitlink metadata cleanup incomplete\")\n   656\t\t}\n   657\t\treturn nil\n   658\t}\n   659\t\n   660\t// reviewGoBuildDir names the temporary build directory the Go toolchain\n   661\t// creates under the TMPDIR the engine gives a review run.\n   662\tvar reviewGoBuildDir = regexp.MustCompile(`^go-build[0-9]+$`)\n   663\t\n   664\t// reviewGoBuildBeforeOpen runs after a go-build name is listed and before it\n   665\t// is opened, reviewGoBuildAfterContents after the directory is emptied and\n   666\t// before its name is checked again, and reviewGoBuildBeforeRemove between that\n   667\t// check and the removal; tests use them to change the name there.\n   668\tvar (\n   669\t\treviewGoBuildBeforeOpen    = func(string) {}\n   670\t\treviewGoBuildAfterContents = func(string) {}\n   671\t\treviewGoBuildBeforeRemove  = func(string) {}\n   672\t)\n   673\t\n   674\t// removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers removes the Go build directories a reviewer's\n   675\t// interrupted `go test` or `go build` left at the top of the run's runtime\n   676\t// directory, each under its own bounded inventory, before the runtime's own\n   677\t// inventory, which a single test binary can exceed (spec\n   678\t// pose-review-cleanup-removes-go-build-leftovers). Only a real directory is\n   679\t// removed; the platform implementation opens it without blocking and only as\n   680\t// a directory, so a link, a FIFO or any other entry stays for the runtime\n   681\t// inventory to judge.\n   682\tfunc removeReviewGoBuildLeftovers(root *os.Root) error {\n   683\t\t// The top level is read in bounded batches and each go-build directory\n   684\t\t// is removed as it is read, so nothing accumulates; only the other\n   685\t\t// entries, which the runtime inventory will judge, count against its\n   686\t\t// bound (review rounds 5 and 6, N6 and N10).\n   687\t\tdir, err := root.Open(\".\")\n   688\t\tif err != nil {\n   689\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n   690\t\t}\n   691\t\tdefer dir.Close()\n   692\t\tothers := 0\n   693\t\tfor {\n   694\t\t\tbatch, err := dir.Readdirnames(256)\n   695\t\t\tfor _, name := range batch {\n   696\t\t\t\tif !reviewGoBuildDir.MatchString(name) {\n   697\t\t\t\t\tothers++\n   698\t\t\t\t\tif others > reviewRuntimeMaxEntries {\n   699\t\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n   700\t\t\t\t\t}\n   701\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   702\t\t\t\t}\n   703\t\t\t\tif err := removeReviewGoBuildDir(root, name); err != nil {\n   704\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n   705\t\t\t\t}\n   706\t\t\t}\n   707\t\t\tif len(batch) == 0 {\n   708\t\t\t\tif err == nil || errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {\n   709\t\t\t\t\treturn nil\n   710\t\t\t\t}\n   711\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n   712\t\t\t}\n   713\t\t}\n   714\t}\n   715\t\n   716\t// reviewRuntimeMaxEntries is the runtime inventory's own entry bound.\n   717\tconst reviewRuntimeMaxEntries = 4096\n   718\t\n   719\tfunc removeReviewOwnedContents(root *os.Root, maxFiles int, maxBytes int64) error {\n   720\t\tpaths := []string{}\n   721\t\tvar total int64\n   722\t\terr := fs.WalkDir(root.FS(), \".\", func(path string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n   723\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   724\t\t\t\treturn err\n   725\t\t\t}\n   726\t\t\tif path == \".\" {\n   727\t\t\t\treturn nil\n   728\t\t\t}\n   729\t\t\tif len(paths) >= maxFiles || strings.Count(path, \"/\") > 128 {\n   730\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup inventory exceeds coverage\")\n   731\t\t\t}\n   732\t\t\tinfo, err := d.Info()\n   733\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   734\t\t\t\treturn err\n   735\t\t\t}\n   736\t\t\tif info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n   737\t\t\t\ttotal += info.Size()\n   738\t\t\t\tif total > maxBytes {\n   739\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cleanup inventory exceeds bytes\")\n   740\t\t\t\t}\n   741\t\t\t}\n   742\t\t\tpaths = append(paths, path)\n   743\t\t\treturn nil\n   744\t\t})\n   745\t\tif err != nil {\n   746\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\")\n   747\t\t}\n   748\t\tfor i := len(paths) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n   749\t\t\tif err := root.Remove(paths[i]); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   750\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"runtime cleanup incomplete; resources retained\")\n   751\t\t\t}\n   752\t\t}\n   753\t\treturn nil\n   754\t}\n   755\t\n   756\tfunc reviewSafetyConflict(run ReviewRun) string {\n   757\t\tif run.Safety == nil {\n   758\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   759\t\t} // Historical runs have no invented observations.\n   760\t\tif run.Safety.SchemaVersion != 1 || (run.Status == ReviewRunCompleted && !run.Safety.CaptureComplete) {\n   761\t\t\treturn \"adapter capture incomplete\"\n   762\t\t}\n   763\t\tif run.Safety.Operation.Outcome != OutcomeCompleted {\n   764\t\t\treturn \"adapter cleanup incomplete\"\n   765\t\t}\n   766\t\treturn \"\"\n   767\t}\n   768\t\n   769\tfunc existingReviewDispatchResult(run ReviewRun) (ReviewRun, error) {\n   770\t\tif run.Safety != nil && run.Safety.Operation.Outcome != OutcomeCompleted {\n   771\t\t\treturn run, fmt.Errorf(\"existing dispatch has incomplete cleanup; no new adapter was started\")\n   772\t\t}\n   773\t\treturn run, nil\n   774\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
